//! The prelude's text, which the compiler reads the builtins from. A module of its own: what a
//! shipped module embeds is asked of its whole text on every load that pulls it, so the one that
//! embeds is small. It lies in the compiler, so the text it embeds is the compiler's input too: a
//! change to `std.prelude` changes what the compiler is built from.

/// The text of `std.prelude`, as the toolchain ships it.
pub fn text() -> Bytes = embed("../std/prelude.ply")
